From 4da1e6b8bdb88fc1d9eadd64740c28a1e3418c7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:16:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] SWGL GPU pixel shading from gecko-w10m (patches 0014-0026,
 0031, 0032, 0034)

SWGL keeps WebRender's vertex shaders on the CPU and hands the fragment
half to a GPU without vertex texture fetch: glsl-to-cxx translates the
fragment shaders, gl.cc sends quads and varyings to the GPU, and a GPU
copy of each texture is kept in step with SWGL's own. Taken from
github.com/Computershik73/gecko-w10m, Direct3D 11 backend as written there.
